# Byte fidelity is a verification requirement in this project, not a preference.
#
# The project verifies sources by SHA-256 and byte size (agent.md V7, H3). Git's
# default end-of-line conversion would rewrite CRLF/LF on checkout and change the
# bytes of a file whose hash was measured and pinned, producing a "drift" that is
# pure tooling artefact. `-text` disables all EOL conversion for every path, so a
# committed file is restored byte-for-byte.
#
# Do not remove this rule, and do not "normalise" a file through Git.
* -text
